      "description": "건축인허가 kind Gold as a table of appended row versions (root ADR-0451, ADR-0564 §6; scripts/ops/gold-versions-build.sh parcel-building-permits → publisher build-parcel-building-permits-versions): gold.parcel_building_permits_versions from the parcel's current 건축인허가 기본개요 rows with their parking by 관리허가대장PK and one list per other file of the permit family (동별개요, 층별개요, 대지위치, 대수선, 가설건축물, 부설주차장, 공작물관리대장, 주택인허가 기본개요 by their own PNU, and 정기점검이력 through the one 표제부 its 관리건축물대장PK names), computed by DuckDB inside the publisher one 시도 at a time and appended as the keys whose digest changed (a removal marker for a key that left), each commit one version_seq. While the lane serves gold.parcel_building_permits it is that table's shadow: it reads the input pins and served edition its foundation-gold-build tag commit recorded, so the takeover verdict (gold-takeover-verdict.sh) compares the two engines over one set of inputs; its first build holds every key. Nothing to do when its inputs, the served parcel edition and its code are the base commit's. A change of the code change table, the served edition or the code rebuilds every PNU; otherwise only the PNUs whose rows (a permit with its parking, a detail row, an inspection's link) or served parcels changed. It starts no Spark; it holds two slots of the host's heavy-work pool, as the lanes' other publisher builds (root ADR-0567: the pool moves with the orchestration, not the engine). Nothing reads it until the lane's takeover PR names it as the lane's gold_table.",
      "systemd_service": "foundation-gold-versions@parcel-building-permits.service",
      "systemd_timer": null,
      "state_paths": [],
      "schedule": "55 10 * * *",
      "started_by": "inputs",
      "stop_grace_minutes": 5,
      "wait_limit_minutes": 0,
